course: dictionary
lesson: 7405
title: A pogrom: a violent attack on a group
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A pogrom is a violent attack by a mob on a group of people. You can work out its meaning from the clues around it. Read «many forces carried out pogroms against Jews». Ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: The words «against Jews» tell you who was attacked. The entry says the group was attacked because of their religion or who they were, not because of anything they had done. That is what makes a pogrom so terrible: innocent people are attacked simply for who they are.
explain: Historians use the word for events in the Russian Empire in the 1800s and early 1900s, and for attacks during the civil war of 1919–1920 in towns that are now in Ukraine. In history, it is the name for a particular kind of event, not for an ordinary fight.
fact: A pogrom is a violent attack by a mob on a group of people.
fact: In a pogrom, people are attacked because of their religion or who they are, and homes and shops are destroyed.
fact: The word was first used for attacks on Jewish people in the Russian Empire in the 1800s and early 1900s.
fact: Kristallnacht in Germany in 1938 was a pogrom against Jews.
fact: History lessons use the word pogrom to show why prejudice and hatred are dangerous.
exercise: «Many forces carried out pogroms against Jews.» What is a pogrom? | *A violent attack by a mob on a group because of who they are | A school trip to a museum | A peaceful meeting to share food | A kind of tall building
exercise: A pogrom attacks people because of their religion or who they are. Why were the people attacked? | Because they had asked for a higher wage | *Because of their religion or who they were, not for anything they had done | Because they had won a race
exercise: «Homes and shops were destroyed and people were hurt.» What does this clue tell you about a pogrom? | A pogrom is a kind of weather | A pogrom is a sports match | *A pogrom is a violent attack that destroys homes and hurts people | A pogrom is a quiet party
test: A pogrom happened in the Russian Empire in the 1800s. What kind of event was it? | A school sports day | A royal wedding | *A cruel, violent attack on innocent people | A peaceful festival
test: Why do history lessons teach about pogroms? | *To show why prejudice and hatred are dangerous | To learn how to bake bread | To count the number of shops | To practise swimming
exam: What does the word pogrom tell a reader about the people who were attacked? | They were the attackers | *They were attacked for who they were, not for anything they had done | They chose to leave their homes | They were lost in the snow
